{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/573157-real-life-fae-incidents","id":573157,"title":"Real-Life \"Fae\" Incidents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-29T14:23:40-07:00","id":573157,"title":"Real-Life \"Fae\" Incidents","content":"With 2e coming out soon, I thought this might be a good topic to put up.<br /> <br /> Now, a number of us here have had strange happenings to us. Perhaps we live in an area historically known for the fae, such as parts of the British Isles. Some of us have had things we couldn't quite call &quot;human&quot; or &quot;animal&quot; appear in our homes, in graveyards, or in forests known being a bit &quot;odd&quot;. Perhaps we've seen strange lights that resemble will-o'-wisps, whether swamp gas or not. To find inspiration for 2e and 2e games: fellow WoD-goers, what are your real-life stories about creatures that may or may have not been the fae, or something analogous to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T15:28:29-07:00","id":573273,"title":"","content":"I once saw a transparent glowing orb. It was about the size of a basketball and had an orange glow. It floated above some trees for about two seconds before vanishing into thin air. I think it was some kind of electrical phenomenon like ball lightning and not aliens, but it's fun to think of it as a fairy or a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T16:12:31-07:00","id":573308,"title":"","content":"My dog sometimes barks and points out the window as if there was something there and we don't see anything. Then when we take her out to show her that there wasn't anything, she will start sniffing a patch of ground real intently and then act confused, as if there really had just been someone or something there, it's fun to think that fairies are involved.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T17:18:31-07:00","id":573333,"title":"","content":"Once I got lost on a really foggy night in my hometown (I was kind of new to driving, at the time), and I turned onto a street whose name I couldn't make out. In the fog and the darkness I couldn't see much of anything, and the street twisted around but didn't seem to have any cross streets. Finally, it emptied out onto a street I knew, and I headed home from there. Not really that weird, but at the time it felt like I had followed some kind of otherworldly shortcut that had taken me just where I needed to go.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I should count myself lucky that nothing came out the bushes on the sides of the road to carry me away to Faerie. ;P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}